Description: drop DEBIAN_TASKS_ONLY=1 to let derivative .desc files surface
Author: Harkirat S Virk <harkiratsvirk@gmail.com>
Origin: local
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-05-15
Bug-Athena: Surfaced 2026-05-15 after the athena-tasksel-data .deb
 (commit 96d7a14) correctly shipped /usr/share/tasksel/descs/athena.desc
 onto /target — but the operator-defined "athena-development-tools"
 and "athena-gnome" tasks STILL never appeared on tasksel's Software-
 selection screen.  Three earlier rounds of debugging chased other
 mechanisms (path probes, mount-on-demand, virtual-package-name
 filtering); the actual filter is one line in pkgsel's postinst.
 .
 Verbatim from upstream `debian/postinst` (line 162):
 .
   DEBIAN_TASKS_ONLY=1 in-target sh -c \
       "tasksel --new-install --debconf-apt-progress='…'" || aptfailed
 .
 The `DEBIAN_TASKS_ONLY=1` env-var is read by tasksel at startup
 (verbatim from upstream `/usr/bin/tasksel:53-65`):
 .
   sub list_task_descs {
       if ($ENV{DEBIAN_TASKS_ONLY}) {
           return glob("$descdir/debian-tasks.desc");
       }
       else {
           return glob("$descdir/*.desc"),
                  glob("$localdescdir/*.desc");
       }
   }
 .
 When set, tasksel ONLY reads `/usr/share/tasksel/descs/debian-tasks.desc`
 — every other `.desc` is silently ignored regardless of content.
 The original Debian rationale (per debian/changelog entry 421) was
 to ensure that during d-i, only the official Debian task set is
 surfaced; third-party tasks added by post-install package
 installations should NOT appear on the first-run task screen.
 .
 That rationale doesn't apply to a Debian DERIVATIVE.  Athena's
 athena-tasksel-data .deb is part of the BASE installation
 (debootstrapped onto every /target via base_include) — its tasks
 represent the operator-defined groups in pkg.list and should
 surface alongside the upstream Debian tasks at first-run, by
 design.  This is the same pattern Ubuntu's `pkgsel` follows
 internally; we apply the equivalent patch here.
 .
 Fix: drop `DEBIAN_TASKS_ONLY=1 ` from the env prefix on the
 tasksel invocation.  Tasksel then reads BOTH
 `/usr/share/tasksel/descs/debian-tasks.desc` (Debian tasks) AND
 `/usr/share/tasksel/descs/athena.desc` (our tasks) and shows the
 union on the Software-selection menu.  No upstream Debian tasks
 are removed; we only stop hiding additional .desc files.
 .
 Why not patch tasksel itself: the env-var check IS the
 documented contract — `DEBIAN_TASKS_ONLY` is a deliberate
 mechanism for callers to opt INTO the restricted view.  pkgsel
 opts in unconditionally (the right call for upstream Debian);
 our derivative needs it OFF.  Patching the caller is the
 contract-respecting fix.
 .
 No security implication.  athena.desc is generated by our
 iso_installer at ISO-build time from the operator's pkg.list
 (commit 96d7a14); shipped via athena-tasksel-data which only
 the system administrator (the operator running build-system.sh)
 controls.  No untrusted third-party can inject tasks.
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/
--- a/debian/postinst
+++ b/debian/postinst
@@ -159,7 +159,7 @@
     log "starting tasksel"
     db_progress INFO pkgsel/progress/tasksel
     apt-install tasksel  # ensure tasksel is installed
-    DEBIAN_TASKS_ONLY=1 in-target sh -c "tasksel --new-install --debconf-apt-progress='--from $tasksel_start --to $tasksel_end --logstderr'" || aptfailed
+    in-target sh -c "tasksel --new-install --debconf-apt-progress='--from $tasksel_start --to $tasksel_end --logstderr'" || aptfailed
 fi

 if db_get pkgsel/include/install-recommends; then
